On May 14, 8:02 am, Topi Linkala <n...@iki.fi> wrote:

> But like I said I don't like to remove the possibility to get quest
> artifacts from bones files. So bones files and wish bringing the owner
> would work together with quite nice rationale.
>
> Bones files containing quest artifacts are far and wide and most of all
> normally not very shallow.

If wishing for quest artifacts were to be forbidden, I wouldn't mind
prohibiting getting them from bones files by treating them the same
way as the invocation items; they would revert to their base state
(credit card, long sword, etc.)

Herein lies another distinction between quest and "ordinary"
artifacts; those from quests are *never* randomly generated in the
dungeon. In fact, the character has to leave the dungeon entirely -
via magic portal to their homeworld - to get it. This is why I don't
think that wishing for someone else's quest item makes sense. But as
that's arguably a "style" issue rather than truly one of gameplay
balance, I made the suggestion of making the conduct rather than
removing the possibility altogether.

